    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "ALLEGHENY AIRLINES\nDC-9\nSEAT BELTS\nPlease keep your seat belt fastened when the seat belt sign is on. When the seat\nbelt sign is turned off in flight, we suggest you keep your seat belt fastened\nwhile seated.\nSEAT BACKS \u0026 SEAT TRAYS\nFederal air regulations require that you place your seat and seat tray in an\nupright position for all takeoffs and landings.\nNO SMOKING\nWhen the no smoking sign is on, extinguish all smoking material. Visable fluid\nlighters are not permitted to be used on the aircraft.\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC EQUIPMENT\nAM, FM, and TV receivers may not be used during flight. These devices may\ndisturb the navigational aids of the aircraft.\nFLOTATION CUSHION\nYour seat cushion is\ndesigned to float.\nGrasp seat cushion and\npull up.\nPROTECTIVE POSITION\nLeave aircraft. Hold\non to straps to keep\nafloat.\nREAR FACING SEAT\nFORWARD FACING SEAT\nRemove eyeglasses and\nsharp objects from\npockets. Fasten seat\nbelt tight and low\nacross hips.\nClasp hands firmly\nbehind head.\nLean back in seat.\nLean forward and down\nas far as possible.\nClasp hands firmly\nunder legs.\nOXYGEN SYSTEM\nIndividual oxygen\nmasks stored in\noverhead panel.\nPanel opens auto-\nmatically. Pull\nmask down.\n(OVER)\nPlace mask over mouth\nand nose. Hook strap\nover head. Breathe\nnormally.",
      "EMERGENCY EXIT INFORMATION\nPLEASE ACQUAINT YOURSELVES WITH THE SAFETY FEATURES\nLOCATED ON THIS AIRCRAFT.\nSHOULD IT BE NECESSARY TO\nEVACUATE THE AIRCRAFT BECAUSE OF AN EMERGENCY, THE\nDIAGRAMS BELOW ILLUSTRATE THE NUMBER OF EXITS FOR YOUR\nUSE.\nFRONT\nDOOR EXITS\nDOOR\nEXITS\nTurn handle forward. Push door out to open.\nOVERWING\nWINDOW\nEXITS\nPULL HANDL\nPull handle to inflate\nslide.\nRemove high heel shoes\n-jump into slide\nwith feet up.\nWINDOW EXITS\nREAR\nAUXILIARY\nEXIT\nTAILCONE\nTAILCONE OPERATION\nPull window in and up. Turn window on side\nand throw out.\nTENT\nDoor Handle Operation\nPULL AND TURN\nOPEN\nTailcone Handle\nOperation\nStep out, slide off\nwing.\nMove away from aircraft quickly.\nRotate Handle\nClockwise\n(Or)\nPULLS\nPull Handle And\nLift Door Inward\nPull Handle To\nRemove Tailcone\n(OVER)\nJULY, 1974\n1D1132717-1\n171-1353"
    ],
